# Bojo — Ollama lane, CPU-ONLY placement (owner requirement, 2026-10-27)
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Bojo is the resident chat / coding / general worker. It must never hold
# dedicated VRAM, because the 16 GB RTX 5080 Laptop is the render GPU: ComfyUI
# and the Qwen3.8-27B IQ3_XXS llama.cpp worker need that memory. `ollama ps`
# reported bojo:latest at "100% GPU" (2.5 GB), i.e. every layer placed in the
# CUDA device buffer. The chat lane passed no num_gpu, so Ollama's automatic
# layer placement decided on its own.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES
# `PARAMETER num_gpu 0` bakes CPU placement into the model definition, so every
# caller (chat, design-studio agent, any ad-hoc client) gets CPU execution even
# when it passes no options at all. This is deliberately a MODEL-level default
# rather than a per-call env knob, because the constraint is a property of the
# model's role on this box, not of one request path.
#
# INSTALL (rebuild in place; reuses the existing blobs, downloads nothing)
#   ollama cp bojo:latest bojo:gpu-orig      # preserve the GPU-placed original
#   ollama create bojo:latest -f scripts/bojo-cpu.Modelfile
#   ollama stop bojo                          # drop the GPU-resident instance
#
# VERIFY
#   ollama ps            -> PROCESSOR column must read "100% CPU"
#   nvidia-smi           -> device used-MiB must not include Bojo's 2.5 GB
#
# Everything else is inherited from bojo:gpu-orig byte-for-byte: TEMPLATE,
# SYSTEM, RENDERER qwen3.5, PARSER qwen3.5, the vision projector layer and the
# Apache-2.0 LICENSE. Only the parameters are restated so this file is readable
# on its own and a future edit cannot silently change two things at once.

FROM bojo:gpu-orig

PARAMETER num_gpu 0
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
PARAMETER num_predict 2048
PARAMETER temperature 0.2
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER presence_penalty 1.5
